rdinated fire missions, and communicated directly with their artillery units. FOOs had the authority to call in fire from their own battery, and from mid-war, some could command fire from their entire regiment. Select officers designated as Commander’s Representatives could even access divisional or corps artillery. This decentralized control allowed for rapid, localized responses in fast-moving operations. Often attached to a company or squadron, FOOs developed quick fire plans involving multiple coordinated targets to support limited offensives. These plans were crucial in assaults and defensive actions, blending artillery firepower with frontline maneuvering. By integrating with supported units and adapting to evolving battlefield demands, FOOs played a central role in the success of British artillery throughout the war."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Homefront","soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3_Cue'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/War_UI/Cues/Drum_Movements/War_UI_Drum_Movement_Field_Snares_3_Cue.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Britain/Homefront/T_forward_observers.T_forward_observers","SubPathString":""},"historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/FORWARD_OBSERVERS.FORWARD_OBSERVERS","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":386.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_event_forward_observers_photo","SourceString":"A British captain briefing a party of forward observers in Normandy, France, June 1944.","LocalizedString":"A British captain briefing a party of forward observers in Normandy, France, June 1944."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_AttackOrder.BP_AttackOrder_C","SubPathString":""}},"variables":[{"name":"unitsToDamage","type":"TArray<int32>","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"didPlayBritishInfantryLastTurn","owner":"card_event_forward_observers_C","params